    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30642" root="عن" body-key="E">
    
      3 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المُعَانَّةُ</span></b>  and 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">العِنَانُ</span></b>  signify <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المُعَارَضَةُ</span>, (S, Msb,
K, TA,) as inf. ns. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَانَّهُ</span> [meaning <i>He did like
as he</i> (the latter) <i>did:</i> or <i>he opposed him, being
opposed by him</i>]. (TA.) See, below, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شِرْكَةُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">العِنَانِ</span>: and also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُنَانَاكَ</span>.

